Startup scripts, configuration and documentation directly related to build VMs within Cloud.
Every image information must be written within its on folder in *images*.
The name of the folder also acts as an ID within the Cloud portal.

# Dependency
Upon updating the repository the file *catalog.yaml* is written to
give an overview of the current images.
In order to achieve this you need to be able to run python 
as well as a couple of python dependencies

* os
* yaml

# How to create a new image

There are 3 types of files

## Documentation.md 
Contains information in markdown on how to use the image

## script.sh 
Contains the script that should be executed on creation.
Within each script there are variables that are set using values from the *configuration.yaml* file

### Will substitute {{version}} to VERSION
Example in configuration.yaml
```
version: VERSION
```
### Will substitute {{packages}} to an array of packages
Example in configuration.yaml
```
packages:
  - PACKAGE1
  - PACKAGE2
  - PACKAGE3 
```
### Will substitute {{users.username}} to an array of usernames, and {{users.password}} to an array of passwords.
BUT also in this case first entry is mandatory and must be set by the user.

Example in configuration.yaml
```
users:
  - username: REQUIRED
    password: REQUIRED
  - username: USER2
    password: PASS2
``` 

### Global parameters

Besides these user defined parameters, there are also a set of global parameters
that can be added to the user script, but their value is set within the portal and should not be user defined.
At the moment these can be set using {{PARAMETER}}
and currently these values can be added...

- project_data
- project_name
- cred_id
- cred_secret
- cloud_domain
- project_domain
- cloud_url

These do not exist in the configuration.yaml file but are global.

## configuration.yaml
General and specific information about the image

Example of mandatory configuration information. This must reside in every configuration file

```
general:
  title: [TITLE]
  category: [CATEGORY]
  base_image: [BASE IMAGE NAME FROM OpenStack]
```

The rest of the configuration file can be filled with configuration for the specific image.
